{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:NuclearInteractions.AlgebraicPrimality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"NuclearInteractions.AlgebraicPrimality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.List"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.one_isAlgebraicallyPrime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.one_isAlgebraicallyPrime","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/algebraic-primality.lean#L35-L48","doc":"**Vacuous primality at `n = 1`.** No nontrivial decomposition can sum to\n`1` (two parts each `≥ 1` already sum to `≥ 2`), so `1` is algebraically prime\nfor any span predicate. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:n-equals-1-vacuous-magic","label":"prop:n-equals-1-vacuous-magic","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/n-equals-1-vacuous-magic.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.IsAlgebraicallyPrime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.IsAlgebraicallyPrime","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/algebraic-primality.lean#L28-L33","doc":"`n` is **algebraically prime** with respect to a span-membership predicate\n`inSpan n parts` (encoding `ψ_n(q) ∈ closed-span of the product over `parts`)\niff `n ≠ 0` and no nontrivial decomposition places `ψ_n` in the corresponding\nspan. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:algebraic-primality","label":"def:algebraic-primality","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/algebraic-primality.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.NontrivialDecomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.NontrivialDecomp","kind":"def","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/algebraic-primality.lean#L23-L26","doc":"A **nontrivial decomposition** of `n`: a list of at least two positive\nparts summing to `n`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}